From 035f858c2c8eda8a454451cb4fdfb1238de209e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mecattaf <thomas@leger.run>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:06:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Disable skinny GEMM on gfx1151

wvSplitK / LLMM1 are pathologically slow on gfx1151 (Strix Halo,
RDNA3.5), so rocm_unquantized_gemm_impl now excludes that arch from the
skinny path and falls back to torch.nn.functional.linear. The existing
VLLM_ROCM_USE_SKINNY_GEMM env var remains the kill-switch for the whole
skinny path; setting it does not re-enable gfx1151.

Also restores the truncated gfx1250 comment the condition had lost.

Manual resolution notes (diff was cut against an older base):
- vllm/model_executor/layers/utils.py applied with offsets +144/+149.
- tests/model_executor/layers/test_rocm_unquantized_gemm.py: upstream
  pins on_gfx1151 -> False in the three tests its base had. This tree has
  three more tests that pin the same gfx predicate set
  (makes_skinny_activation_contiguous,
  makes_llmm1_activation_contiguous,
  rejects_unsupported_skinny_layouts); all six are pinned here, since an
  unpinned predicate would make them fail when the suite is actually run
  on gfx1151 hardware. noncontiguous_activation_real_kernel pins no gfx
  predicates and is left alone.

Cherry-picked-from: vllm-project/vllm#51511
